  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Evaluation of the Archdiocese of Lusaka - Reducing Stigma, Responding to HIV project</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project aimed to mitigate the impact of HIV by improving the quality of life of people living with HIV and reducing vulnerability to new HIV infections in urban, peri-urban and rural Lusaka Province and the Central Province of Zambia.

This project was holistic in addressing the major HIV challenges, which include stigma. The four specific areas of action were: 
1. Reduce stigma and discrimination against PLHIV;
2. Improve knowledge, attitudes and practices around HIV prevention;
3. Increase access to services and support;
4. Increase access to entrepreneurial training, savings and lending opportunities.</narrative>
  </description>
